.TH SDL_HINT_KEYCODE_OPTIONS 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_KEYCODE_OPTIONS \- A variable that controls keycode representation in keyboard events.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_KEYCODE_OPTIONS \(dqSDL_KEYCODE_OPTIONS\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This variable is a comma separated set of options for translating keycodes in events:
.PP

\(bu \(dqnone\(dq: Keycode options are cleared, this overrides other options\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqhide_numpad\(dq: The numpad keysyms will be translated into their non-numpad versions based on the current NumLock state\[char46] For example,
.BR SDLK_KP_4
would become
.BR SDLK_4
if
.BR SDL_KMOD_NUM
is set in the event modifiers, and
.BR SDLK_LEFT
if it is unset\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqfrench_numbers\(dq: The number row on French keyboards is inverted, so pressing the 1 key would yield the keycode
.BR SDLK_1 ,
or \(aq1\(aq, instead of
.BR SDLK_AMPERSAND ,
or \(aq&\(aq
.PP
\(bu \(dqlatin_letters\(dq: For keyboards using non-Latin letters, such as Russian or Thai, the letter keys generate keycodes as though it had an English QWERTY layout\[char46] e\[char46]g\[char46] pressing the key associated with
.BR SDL_SCANCODE_A
on a Russian keyboard would yield \(aqa\(aq instead of a Cyrillic letter\[char46]
.PP
The default value for this hint is \(dqfrench_numbers,latin_letters\(dq
.PP
Some platforms like Emscripten only provide modified keycodes and the options are not used\[char46]
.PP
These options do not affect the return value of
.BR SDL_GetKeyFromScancode ()
or
.BR SDL_GetScancodeFromKey (),
they just apply to the keycode included in key events\[char46]
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

